"""
# std.error — Standard Error Type

SimpleError is the standard error type carried by SFFI wrapper functions
(net, fs, tcp, etc.) in their `Result<T, SimpleError>` returns.

It is a plain Simple class, NOT a builtin runtime type. It was declared
`extern class` until 2026-09-13, which made the constructor unresolvable —
`error("boom")` failed with `E1002: function `SimpleError` not found`, because
`extern class` registers no constructor. There is no `SimpleError` in
`src/runtime/**` or in the frontend, and nothing outside Simple ever produces
an instance: every value comes from `error(...)` below. Do not restore
`extern` here. See
`doc/08_tracking/bug/extern_class_constructor_not_found_simpleerror_2026-08-02.md`.
"""

class SimpleError:
    """Error payload for SFFI wrapper `Result<T, SimpleError>` returns."""
    message: text
    code: i32

pub fn error(message: text) -> SimpleError:
    """Construct a SimpleError with the given message and code 0."""
    SimpleError(message: message, code: 0)

export SimpleError, error
